    "edit": {
        "tabs": {
            "quickStart": {
                "heading": "Add Daon TrustX Authenticator",
                "subHeading": "Follow the steps below to add Daon TrustX login (re-verification) to your application.",
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "title": "Configure the connection",
                        "content": "<p>Select the <strong>Daon Identity Verifier</strong> connection and provide the <strong>Login Process Definition</strong> on the <strong>Settings</strong> tab. The OIDC client credentials, endpoints and scopes are resolved from the referenced Daon Identity Verifier connection.</p>"
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Map attributes",
                        "content": "<p>On the <strong>Attributes</strong> tab, map Daon verified claims (e.g. <Code class=\"inline-code\">given_name</Code>, <Code class=\"inline-code\">family_name</Code>, <Code class=\"inline-code\">birthdate</Code>) to WSO2 local claims. These drive verification.</p>"
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Add Daon TrustX to a login flow",
                        "content": "<p>Add this <strong>Daon TrustX Authenticator</strong> to an application's <strong>Login Flow</strong> as a step after the user is identified, to re-verify users already enrolled with the referenced Daon Identity Verifier. Enrolment (registration / invited-user) is driven by the Daon Identity Verifier connection itself.</p>"
                    }
                ]
            },
